[5] A. Giazitzis & E. N. Zois, "SigmML: Metric meta-learning for Writer Independent Offline Signature Verification in the Space of SPD Matrices," 2024 IEEE/CVF Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision (WACV), pp. 6300-6310, 2024. DOI: 10.1109/WACV57701.2024.00619
[6] A. Giazitzis, M. Diaz, E. N. Zois, & M. A. Ferrer, "Janus-Faced Handwritten Signature Attack: A Clash Between a Handwritten Signature Duplicator and a Writer Independent Metric Meta-learning Offline Signature Verifier," Proc. ICDAR 2024, Springer Nature Switzerland, pp. 216-232, 2024. DOI: 10.1007/978-3-031-70536-6_13

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENT NOTICES AND CITATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Manopt (v8.0)
This software incorporates components from the Manopt toolbox (https://www.manopt.org).
Citation: Boumal, N., Mishra, B., Absil, P.-A., and Sepulchre, R., "Manopt, a Matlab Toolbox for Optimization on Manifolds", Journal of Machine Learning Research, 15 (2014), 1455-1459.

2. Recursive K-means & Karcher Mean Implementation (`kmeans_KarcherMean`)
This software incorporates algorithmic implementations for recursive Karcher expectation estimation and K-means over symmetric positive definite (SPD) manifolds.
Citations:
- G. Cheng, H. Salehian, B. C. Vemuri, “Efficient Recursive Algorithms for Computing the Mean Diffusion Tensor and Applications to DTI Segmentation”, ECCV 2012.
- J. Ho, G. Cheng, H. Salehian, B. C. Vemuri, “Recursive Karcher Expectation Estimators And Geometric Law of Large Numbers”, AISTATS 2013.
- H. Salehian, G. Cheng, B. C. Vemuri, J. Ho, “Recursive Estimation of the Stein Center of SPD Matrices & its Applications”, ICCV 2013.

3. Discriminative Alpha-Beta Divergence for Positive Definite Matrices
This software incorporates code implementing the discriminative alpha-beta divergence.
Citation: A. Cherian, P. Stanitsas, M. Harandi, V. Morellas, and N. Papanikolopoulos, "Learning Discriminative Alpha-Beta Divergence for Positive Definite Matrices", ICCV, 2017.
License Terms: Copyright (c) 2017, Panagiotis Stanitsas and Anoop Cherian. All rights reserved. Distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License (see terms below).

4. Signature Verification Evaluation Framework (`sigver_wiwd`)
This software incorporates components from the sigver_wiwd toolkit (https://github.com/luizgh/sigver_wiwd) for the evaluation/testing stage.
Citations:
- Hafemann, L. G., Sabourin, R., and Oliveira, L. S. "Learning Features for Offline Handwritten Signature Verification using Deep Convolutional Neural Networks", Pattern Recognition, 2017.
- Hafemann, L. G., Sabourin, R., and Oliveira, L. S. "Fixed-sized representation learning from Offline Handwritten Signatures of different sizes", International Journal on Document Analysis and Recognition (IJDAR), 2018.
License Terms: Distributed under the BSD 2-Clause License (see terms below). Note that associated trained models may carry non-commercial restrictions due to the underlying GPDS dataset.

